+// in display order, and the pager shows a viewport onto that strip at a
+// fractional position. At rest the strip holds only the visible space. A
+// switch by command or click adds the target space next to the visible pages
+// and animates the position; a swipe moves the position with the fingers.
+// The window always shows the space of the active tab in the real page, so a
+// switch activates the target space at the moment it is decided (when a
+// command starts, when the fingers lift), and the real and peek pages trade
+// places in the same frame without moving anything on screen.
